a. fast, safe, and empathetic;
b. coordination between government agencies;
c. guarantee of confidentiality;
d. easily accessible; and
e. free of charge.

Article 16
(1) The Regional Government through the Office/UPTD is obligated to conduct empowerment in the economic field for victims of acts of violence, exploitation and neglect.
(2) Forms of empowerment for victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), include:
a. providing the necessary requirements for entrepreneurship training for victims of acts of violence, in order to increase knowledge, attitude, and business skills;
b. facilitating the implementation of various job training and skills training;
c. conducting assistance in developing productive economic enterprises;
d. exploring cooperation with small, medium and large companies, as well as financial institutions to develop the businesses of victims of acts of violence;
e. endeavoring to provide capital for victims of acts of violence; and
f. expanding access to information and promoting the products of victims of acts of violence.

